      "content": "Your pain feels fundamental because your trauma is deep, but let go is often what happens when we stop fighting because we're too exhausted to try. Even if the darkness seems permanent right now, choose to step out of your head and into a room where someone at a hospital or crisis line can hold you while the urge to disappear crashes over you. Fight the fight for your life until you find the light that isn't hiding under your mask or pretending to be nice. Your existence has meaning, even if you cannot see how right at this moment or when.",
